{"acceleration_structures":[],"air_sha256":"e7d7f40f09b6f5c7735a4473868e5f61fa62429c2fb5432dcbf64c7f0bbf3e8a","argument_buffer_buffers":[],"argument_buffer_intersection_function_tables":[],"argument_buffer_textures":[],"authored_by":"claude:opus-5","buffers":[{"binding":0,"initial_bytes_b64":"ZAAAAGUAAABmAAAAZwAAAGgAAABpAAAAagAAAGsAAABsAAAAbQAAAG4AAABvAAAAcAAAAHEAAAByAAAAcwAAAA==","role":"in_out"},{"binding":1,"initial_bytes_b64":"yAAAAMkAAADKAAAAywAAAMwAAADNAAAAzgAAAM8AAADQAAAA0QAAANIAAADTAAAA1AAAANUAAADWAAAA1wAAAA==","role":"in_out"},{"binding":2,"initial_bytes_b64":"LAEAAC0BAAAuAQAALwEAADABAAAxAQAAMgEAADMBAAA0AQAANQEAADYBAAA3AQAAOAEAADkBAAA6AQAAOwEAAA==","role":"in_out"},{"binding":3,"initial_bytes_b64":"zc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3Nzc3NzQ==","role":"output"}],"case_id":"69bf22a204845713077fda5d813e93db782e9c2f353e84aa7d9d477be2d3af28","compare":{"kind":"exact"},"device_buffer_arrays":[],"dispatch":{"grid":[8,1,1],"threads_per_threadgroup":[8,1,1]},"entry":"chained_pointer_selects","execution_safety":"loop_free","function_constants":[],"intersection_function_tables":[],"kernel_stage_inputs":[],"name":"replay-a-chained-pointer-select-through-a-load-and-a-store","output":{"binding":3,"kind":"buffer","length":160,"offset":0},"rationale":"A pointer selected between two descriptors and then selected AGAIN against a third, so one select's arm is itself a selected pointer. Logical SPIR-V has no pointer value that can be any of three descriptors, so the emitter cannot merge them: it builds a SELECTED ACCESS TREE and replays every consumer once per leaf under the branch condition that selects it. Coverage, measured with llvm-cov over all 959 corpus-backed cased sources and all public fixtures: this one module reaches NINE functions no authored case or fixture reaches -- build_selected_access_tree and build_selected_access_arm in select_gep.rs, and emit_selected_access_tree_load, emit_selected_access_tree_load_value, emit_selected_access_arm_load_value, emit_selected_access_tree_store, emit_selected_access_tree_store_with_parent, emit_selected_access_arm_store and selected_access_branch_condition in raw_select.rs. That is the whole tree build plus both replay directions; select_gep.rs was 12 of 15 functions uncovered before this. The STORE row is what makes the replay observable. A store through a merged pointer is a read-modify-write on EVERY arm: the chosen descriptor gets the new value and each other descriptor gets its own bytes written back unchanged. Lane gid writes 500+gid into slot gid+8 of whichever buffer q names -- a slot no other lane touches, so there is no race -- and then reads slot gid+8 of all three buffers. Exactly one of the last three rows may show 500+gid on each lane and the other two must still hold their initial values, so an arm confusion moves a marker into the wrong row and a read-modify-write that writes a constant instead of the old value destroys the untouched ones. a holds 100+i, b holds 200+i, c holds 300+i; p is a on odd lanes and b on even, q is p on lanes 0-3 and c on lanes 4-7. Derived before running: out[0..7]=200 101 202 103 304 305 306 307; out[8..15]=201 101 201 101 301 301 301 301; out[16..23]=108 501 110 503 112 113 114 115; out[24..31]=500 209 502 211 212 213 214 215; out[32..39]=308 309 310 311 504 505 506 507. Every value is an exact small integer, so nothing depends on rounding.","render_targets":[],"samplers":[],"stage":"kernel","texture_arrays":[],"textures":[],"threadgroup_memory":[],"vertex_inputs":[],"visible_function_references":[],"visible_function_tables":[]}
